      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose of metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of serious GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a more typical regimen\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give me a reason for the order note. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
